WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:10.135
Ready?

00:00:10.135 --> 00:00:12.011
yeah. You good? okay.

00:00:15.306 --> 00:00:16.558
While we were shooting Swagger,

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:18.393
the world changed.

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:22.355
In 2020 people really started to lean in

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:23.773
and ask themselves

00:00:23.773 --> 00:00:25.775
why there's certain things in the country

00:00:25.775 --> 00:00:27.193
that happen in the way that they do,

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.529
that they've been happening for such a long time.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.156
There was a lot of social issues that

00:00:31.156 --> 00:00:32.866
arose during the pandemic.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:35.493
when things pause and things shut down and the

00:00:35.493 --> 00:00:37.162
social issues came into play

00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:39.164
Reggie put those at the forefront

00:00:39.164 --> 00:00:41.249
because they were things that he wanted to show

00:00:41.249 --> 00:00:42.959
that we weren't scared to talk about

00:00:42.959 --> 00:00:47.922
I can't breathe, I can't breathe, I can't breathe

00:00:47.922 --> 00:00:48.631
I really

00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:51.176
had to ask myself, ya know, do I wanna deal with this?

00:00:51.176 --> 00:00:53.970
but it just really occurred to me that this was another

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:57.932
opportunity to hold a mirror up to, to society

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:06.232
The ability to add current events into a s how

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.735
to make them more more powerful ya know,

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.570
they hit a little closer to home

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:13.114
the stuff that goes on in our every day lives,

00:01:13.114 --> 00:01:13.740
we need to see,

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.950
even though it's a tough conversations to have

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.870
What we speak on in the show

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:21.873
are things that young people are

00:01:21.873 --> 00:01:23.666
going through all over the country

00:01:23.666 --> 00:01:27.921
that are unseen and it will mold you or it will break you

00:01:29.839 --> 00:01:34.385
Our kids go out of town and are confronted by racism.

00:01:34.385 --> 00:01:35.428
Something wrong, officers?

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:36.971
We got a call about a disturbance

00:01:36.971 --> 00:01:40.225
We're just a basketball team on the way to our game

00:01:40.225 --> 00:01:41.559
We're gonna need to see some ID

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:44.062
No matter if you're a star basketball player

00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:46.564
or you work a regular job, that stuff may happen to you

00:01:46.564 --> 00:01:49.359
We wanted to see what would happen

00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:53.154
if they had different points of view about how to address

00:01:53.154 --> 00:01:53.863
the issue

00:01:54.155 --> 00:01:56.157
What would you want me to do? Brawl wit em?

00:01:56.157 --> 00:01:58.201
We shoulda told them that we weren't scared.

00:01:58.201 --> 00:02:00.203
I was scared.

00:02:00.995 --> 00:02:03.540
Now are we allowed to in this country

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:07.460
still have different points of view and still be American?

00:02:08.336 --> 00:02:12.006
What happens if someone takes a knee during the flag

00:02:12.715 --> 00:02:14.968
and other people have different points of view?

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:18.555
Are we allowed to love this country and challenge it?

00:02:18.847 --> 00:02:19.931
What does it matter?

00:02:19.931 --> 00:02:21.599
It matters No it doesn't

00:02:21.599 --> 00:02:23.143
I'm talkin 'bout brotherhood

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:24.143
If I kneel,

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:25.353
if I stand.

00:02:26.271 --> 00:02:27.564
It's not gonna change how you all see me.

00:02:28.439 --> 00:02:29.399
 Or how you all treat me.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:35.613
Reggie put into us a responsibility as performers

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:38.157
to be a voice for the voiceless

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.869
and uh to inspire people to be better

00:02:40.952 --> 00:02:42.412
If people can't hear you,

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:43.705
you can't change them.

00:02:44.038 --> 00:02:45.123
They weren't tryin to hear us.

00:02:45.123 --> 00:02:46.833
Scream loud enough and they will hear us.

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:49.919
Scream loud enough and they'll hear 6'4" &amp; black

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:51.504
I think what we did was right

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.464
when we wrote all of that into the series and

00:02:53.464 --> 00:02:55.925
cuz this is a dialogue that we need to have as a country

00:02:55.925 --> 00:02:57.135
to speak on

00:02:57.302 --> 00:03:01.306
things like police brutality or the pandemic in general

00:03:01.306 --> 00:03:03.016
and how it affected people

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:05.727
it makes what you're doing honorable

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:08.187
inspiration is the most powerful thing

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:10.315
that we got on the planet.

00:03:10.315 --> 00:03:11.524
In this day in age,

00:03:11.941 --> 00:03:12.775
in this time

00:03:13.568 --> 00:03:15.945
what it means to grow up Black in America

00:03:15.945 --> 00:03:17.989
Is a question that we need to ask

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:21.784
and I think our show will not give all the answers but

00:03:21.784 --> 00:03:24.454
ideally it'll provoke the right questions

00:03:24.829 --> 00:03:26.789
I wanna get the audience at the edge of their seat

00:03:27.624 --> 00:03:29.709
and while they're leaning forward, hit em with the truth.

